      "message": "The message talks about GICv4 and VLPIs, but this branch also clears has_direct_lpi, which is a GICv3 feature, and I think that one deserves a sentence of its own because it is not free.\n\nClearing it removes the only writers of GICR_INVLPIR and GICR_INVALLR in the tree, so every enable_irq and irq_set_affinity on an LPI goes through the emulated ITS command queue instead of one MMIO write and a GICR_SYNCR poll. On a DirectLPI SoC that is a real cost coming out of a commit whose stated purpose is turning off GICv4. It also means the two INV patches are hardening against a malicious host only, which is not how their commit messages read.\n\nIs clearing the third flag deliberate?",
